.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NETSTAT 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm netstat
.Nd show the live socket table and interface counters
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a
.Op Fl i | Fl s
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the live network state through the
.Dq net:
control channel. With no options it prints the socket table and then the per-interface packet
and byte counters.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Print only the live socket table.
.It Fl i
Print only the interface counters.
.It Fl s
Print only the interface counters.
.El
.Pp
Every socket row carries the transport (tcp, udp or icmp), the state, the local endpoint, the peer
when connected, the interface, and the receive and transmit queue sizes. Every counter row carries
the received and transmitted packet and byte counts, receive and transmit errors, and receive and
transmit drops, all as reported by
.Xr netd 8 .
Rows and counters are never fabricated: when the server does not expose counters for an
interface, the tool prints
.Dq counters unavailable
instead of a zero row.
.Pp
No raw socket is opened and no kernel memory is read directly.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ping 8 ,
.Xr route 8 ,
.Xr netd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
